Thanks, I incorrectly assumed that fixed.x would exclude sch from the observed variables.

As I briefly mentioned in the original post, the model below neutralizes the effect of sch, so that the difference test with hsm1 has 1 df:

hsm6    <-  ' visual  =~ x1 + x2 + x3

              textual =~ x4 + x5 + x6
              speed   =~ x7 + x8 + x9

              visual ~ 0*sch '

But, in my case, it is probably more intuitive to treat sch as a grouping variable, with some parameters constrained to be equal across the two groups.  While the above models and data wouldn't indicate it, these issues are relevant to framing a repeated measures ANOVA as an SEM.

Ed

