Message-ID: <ezx9ISQRBpA.ioyQvEDiYHQJ@lavaan.groups.google.com>
In-Reply-To: <ezx9ISQRBpA.Xmp2S_bH68kJ@lavaan.groups.google.com>
References: <ezx9ISQRBpA.Xmp2S_bH68kJ@lavaan.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/lavaan/c/ezx9ISQRBpA/m/ioyQvEDiYHQJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

     The “BY” syntax in the Mplus codes implies a higher order factor, but I think that is a mistake.  You do have to fix its variance and force it to be orthogonal to F1, but I think your task is simpler than this, as long as you directly fix the parameters that need fixing.

F1 =~ ind11 + ind12 + ind13
F2 =~ ind21 + ind22 + ind23
F3 =~ ind31 + ind32 + ind33

F2 ~ F1 + F2_residual
F2 ~~ 0*F2
F2_residual ~~ 1*F2_residual

F2_residual ~~ 0*F1

F3 ~ F2_residual + F1

I would expect this to work.

--Ed Rigdon

