On 10/22/2014 01:09 PM, Edward Rigdon wrote:
> does fixing a formative weight to 1 also prevent default standardization

> of the factor, in the sem and cfa functions?

No. I am afraid there is nothing intelligent about the "<~" operator...
In fact, I would recommend not using it. If you write:

f =~ 0
f ~ 1*x2 +x2 + x3
f ~~ 0*f

nothing is hidden, and you have more flexibility.

Yves.

