Terry,

Thanks for this interesting post. Your solution is quite elegant. Problem with my real data set, however, is that I have 18 "plots" each with only 5 data points... So this then would become a 18-group analysis, with not enough data per plot for a meaningful analysis.
Another thought that crossed my mind was to just get residuals per plot a priori, and then go ahead and run the SEM on these residuals. Maybe a bit crude, but then at least the variation among plots is taken care of?

